# ECharts for React: Tips & Tricks Guide
## Making Your Charts Beautiful & Avoiding Common Pitfalls

---

## 🎨 Making ECharts Beautiful (Not Boring!)

### 1. **Use Built-in Themes** (Easiest Win)

ECharts has several built-in themes that are WAY better than the defaults:

```jsx
import ReactECharts from 'echarts-for-react';

// Available themes: 'light', 'dark', 'vintage', 'macarons', 'infographic', 'shine', 'roma'
<ReactECharts 
  option={chartOption} 
  theme="dark"  // or "macarons" for colorful, "vintage" for muted
/>
```

**Quick wins:**
- **`dark`** - Professional, modern look
- **`macarons`** - Colorful, friendly (like Recharts vibes)
- **`vintage`** - Muted, sophisticated
- **`shine`** - Glossy, polished

### 2. **Create Custom Themes** (Next Level)

Use the [**ECharts Theme Builder**](https://echarts.apache.org/en/theme-builder.html) - it's a visual editor:

```jsx
import customTheme from './my-theme.json';
import * as echarts from 'echarts';

// Register your theme
echarts.registerTheme('my-custom', customTheme);

// Use it
<ReactECharts option={option} theme="my-custom" />
```

### 3. **Add Gradients** (Instant Polish)

```jsx
const option = {
  series: [{
    type: 'bar',
    data: [120, 200, 150, 80],
    itemStyle: {
      color: {
        type: 'linear',
        x: 0, y: 0, x2: 0, y2: 1,  // Top to bottom
        colorStops: [
          { offset: 0, color: '#83bff6' },
          { offset: 0.5, color: '#188df0' },
          { offset: 1, color: '#188df0' }
        ]
      }
    }
  }]
};
```

**Area chart gradients** (looks amazing):
```jsx
series: [{
  type: 'line',
  areaStyle: {
    color: {
      type: 'linear',
      x: 0, y: 0, x2: 0, y2: 1,
      colorStops: [
        { offset: 0, color: 'rgba(58, 77, 233, 0.8)' },
        { offset: 1, color: 'rgba(58, 77, 233, 0.1)' }
      ]
    }
  }
}]
```

### 4. **Shadows & Depth** (Professional Touch)

```jsx
itemStyle: {
  shadowBlur: 10,
  shadowColor: 'rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3)',
  shadowOffsetY: 5,
  borderRadius: [5, 5, 0, 0]  // Rounded top corners
}
```

### 5. **Better Color Palettes**

Don't use the default colors! Try these curated palettes:

```jsx
// Modern & Clean
color: ['#5470c6', '#91cc75', '#fac858', '#ee6666', '#73c0de', '#3ba272']

// Vibrant
color: ['#fc5c65', '#fd9644', '#fed330', '#26de81', '#2bcbba', '#eb3b5a']

// Professional Business
color: ['#003f5c', '#58508d', '#bc5090', '#ff6361', '#ffa600']

// Pastel (trendy)
color: ['#a8dadc', '#457b9d', '#1d3557', '#f1faee', '#e63946']
```

Apply globally:
```jsx
const option = {
  color: ['#fc5c65', '#fd9644', '#fed330', '#26de81'],
  // ... rest of config
};
```

### 6. **Typography Matters**

```jsx
title: {
  text: 'Sales Dashboard',
  textStyle: {
    fontSize: 24,
    fontWeight: 'normal',  // or 'bold'
    fontFamily: 'Arial, sans-serif',
    color: '#333'
  },
  subtextStyle: {
    fontSize: 14,
    color: '#999'
  }
}
```

### 7. **Grid Spacing** (More Breathing Room)

Default spacing is cramped. Fix it:

```jsx
grid: {
  left: '3%',
  right: '4%',
  bottom: '3%',
  top: '15%',
  containLabel: true  // Prevents label cutoff
}
```

### 8. **Smooth Lines** (Much Nicer)

```jsx
series: [{
  type: 'line',
  smooth: true,  // Curves instead of hard angles
  smoothMonotone: 'x'  // Maintains monotonicity
}]
```

### 9. **Emphasis Effects** (Interactive Polish)

```jsx
emphasis: {
  focus: 'series',  // Highlight entire series on hover
  blurScope: 'coordinateSystem',
  itemStyle: {
    shadowBlur: 20,
    shadowColor: 'rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)'
  }
}
```

### 10. **Legends & Tooltips** (Better UX)

```jsx
legend: {
  orient: 'horizontal',
  top: 'bottom',
  icon: 'circle',  // instead of default rectangle
  itemGap: 20,
  textStyle: {
    fontSize: 14,
    color: '#666'
  }
},
tooltip: {
  trigger: 'axis',
  backgroundColor: 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95)',
  borderColor: '#ccc',
  borderWidth: 1,
  textStyle: {
    color: '#333'
  },
  axisPointer: {
    type: 'shadow',  // or 'line', 'cross'
    shadowStyle: {
      color: 'rgba(150, 150, 150, 0.1)'
    }
  }
}
```

---

## ⚠️ Common Pitfalls & How to Avoid Them

### **PITFALL #1: Chart Re-renders on Every Component Render** ❌

**Problem:** Creating option object inline causes flicker and lag.

```jsx
// ❌ BAD - Creates new object every render
function MyChart() {
  return <ReactECharts option={{
    xAxis: { data: ['Mon', 'Tue'] },
    series: [{ data: [120, 200] }]
  }} />;
}
```

**Solution:** Use `useMemo`!

```jsx
// ✅ GOOD - Memoized, only recreates when data changes
function MyChart({ data }) {
  const option = useMemo(() => ({
    xAxis: { data: data.labels },
    series: [{ data: data.values }]
  }), [data]);

  return <ReactECharts option={option} />;
}
```

### **PITFALL #2: Not Tree-Shaking** ❌

**Problem:** Full ECharts bundle is huge (~800KB+)

```jsx
// ❌ BAD - Imports everything
import * as echarts from 'echarts';
```

**Solution:** Import only what you need

```jsx
// ✅ GOOD - Import specific modules
import * as echarts from 'echarts/core';
import { LineChart, BarChart } from 'echarts/charts';
import { GridComponent, TooltipComponent } from 'echarts/components';
import { CanvasRenderer } from 'echarts/renderers';

echarts.use([LineChart, BarChart, GridComponent, TooltipComponent, CanvasRenderer]);

import ReactEChartsCore from 'echarts-for-react/lib/core';

<ReactEChartsCore echarts={echarts} option={option} />
```

**Bundle savings:** Can reduce from 800KB to ~200-400KB!

### **PITFALL #3: Responsiveness Not Automatic** ❌

**Problem:** Charts don't resize with window

```jsx
// ❌ BAD - Fixed size
<ReactECharts option={option} style={{ width: 600, height: 400 }} />
```

**Solution:** Use percentage-based sizing

```jsx
// ✅ GOOD - Responsive
<ReactECharts 
  option={option} 
  style={{ width: '100%', height: '400px' }}
  opts={{ renderer: 'canvas' }}  // Canvas performs better
/>
```

Or use the `autoResize` prop (enabled by default in echarts-for-react):
```jsx
<ReactECharts option={option} autoResize={true} />
```

### **PITFALL #4: Tooltip/Label Text Overflow** ❌

**Problem:** Long text gets cut off

**Solution:**
```jsx
tooltip: {
  confine: true,  // Keeps tooltip inside chart bounds
  formatter: (params) => {
    // Custom formatting for long text
    return `${params.name}: ${params.value}`;
  }
},
xAxis: {
  axisLabel: {
    rotate: 45,  // Rotate long labels
    interval: 0,  // Show all labels (not just some)
    formatter: (value) => {
      return value.length > 10 ? value.slice(0, 10) + '...' : value;
    }
  }
}
```

### **PITFALL #5: Not Handling Loading States** ❌

**Solution:** Use the `showLoading` prop

```jsx
function MyChart({ isLoading, data }) {
  return (
    <ReactECharts 
      option={chartOption}
      showLoading={isLoading}
      loadingOption={{
        text: 'Loading...',
        color: '#4ea397',
        maskColor: 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8)'
      }}
    />
  );
}
```

### **PITFALL #6: Poor Performance with Large Datasets** ❌

**Solutions:**

1. **Use Canvas instead of SVG:**
```jsx
<ReactECharts option={option} opts={{ renderer: 'canvas' }} />
```

2. **Enable data sampling:**
```jsx
series: [{
  type: 'line',
  sampling: 'lttb',  // Largest-Triangle-Three-Buckets algorithm
  large: true,
  largeThreshold: 2000
}]
```

3. **Progressive rendering:**
```jsx
series: [{
  progressive: 1000,  // Render 1000 points at a time
  progressiveThreshold: 3000
}]
```

### **PITFALL #7: Animations on Every Update** ❌

**Problem:** Charts animate every time data updates (annoying in dashboards)

**Solution:**
```jsx
// Disable animations for updates, keep for initial render
const option = {
  animation: true,  // Initial animation
  animationDuration: 750,
  animationEasing: 'cubicOut'
};

// On update, use notMerge: false to avoid re-animation
<ReactECharts option={option} notMerge={false} />
```

Or conditionally disable:
```jsx
series: [{
  animation: isInitialRender,  // Only animate on first load
  animationDuration: 500
}]
```

---

## 🚀 React-Specific Best Practices

### **1. Create Reusable Chart Components**

```jsx
// components/LineChart.jsx
import React, { useMemo } from 'react';
import ReactECharts from 'echarts-for-react';

export function LineChart({ data, title, color = '#5470c6' }) {
  const option = useMemo(() => ({
    title: { text: title },
    xAxis: { 
      type: 'category',
      data: data.labels 
    },
    yAxis: { type: 'value' },
    series: [{
      data: data.values,
      type: 'line',
      smooth: true,
      itemStyle: { color }
    }]
  }), [data, title, color]);

  return <ReactECharts option={option} style={{ height: 400 }} />;
}
```

### **2. Handle Events Properly**

```jsx
const onChartClick = (params) => {
  console.log('Clicked:', params);
  // params.name, params.value, params.dataIndex
};

<ReactECharts 
  option={option}
  onEvents={{
    'click': onChartClick,
    'legendselectchanged': (params) => console.log(params)
  }}
/>
```

### **3. Access Chart Instance**

```jsx
function MyChart() {
  const chartRef = useRef(null);

  const handleResetZoom = () => {
    const instance = chartRef.current.getEchartsInstance();
    instance.dispatchAction({
      type: 'restore'  // Reset zoom
    });
  };

  return (
    <>
      <button onClick={handleResetZoom}>Reset Zoom</button>
      <ReactECharts ref={chartRef} option={option} />
    </>
  );
}
```

### **4. TypeScript Support**

```tsx
import type { EChartsOption } from 'echarts';

const option: EChartsOption = {
  xAxis: { type: 'category', data: ['A', 'B'] },
  yAxis: { type: 'value' },
  series: [{ type: 'bar', data: [10, 20] }]
};
```

---

## 📊 Quick Wins for Common Chart Types

### **Bar Chart - Modern Look**

```jsx
{
  xAxis: { type: 'category', data: ['Mon', 'Tue', 'Wed'] },
  yAxis: { type: 'value' },
  series: [{
    type: 'bar',
    data: [120, 200, 150],
    barWidth: '60%',  // Not too thin
    itemStyle: {
      borderRadius: [5, 5, 0, 0],
      color: {
        type: 'linear',
        x: 0, y: 0, x2: 0, y2: 1,
        colorStops: [
          { offset: 0, color: '#667eea' },
          { offset: 1, color: '#764ba2' }
        ]
      }
    }
  }]
}
```

### **Line Chart - Smooth & Elegant**

```jsx
{
  xAxis: { 
    type: 'category', 
    data: dates,
    boundaryGap: false  // Start from edge
  },
  yAxis: { type: 'value' },
  series: [{
    type: 'line',
    data: values,
    smooth: true,
    symbol: 'circle',
    symbolSize: 8,
    lineStyle: { width: 3 },
    areaStyle: {
      color: {
        type: 'linear',
        x: 0, y: 0, x2: 0, y2: 1,
        colorStops: [
          { offset: 0, color: 'rgba(88, 80, 236, 0.4)' },
          { offset: 1, color: 'rgba(88, 80, 236, 0.0)' }
        ]
      }
    }
  }]
}
```

### **Pie Chart - 3D Effect**

```jsx
{
  series: [{
    type: 'pie',
    radius: ['40%', '70%'],  // Donut
    avoidLabelOverlap: true,
    itemStyle: {
      borderRadius: 10,
      borderColor: '#fff',
      borderWidth: 2
    },
    label: {
      show: true,
      formatter: '{b}: {d}%'
    },
    emphasis: {
      label: { show: true, fontSize: 16 },
      itemStyle: {
        shadowBlur: 10,
        shadowOffsetX: 0,
        shadowColor: 'rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)'
      }
    },
    data: [
      { value: 1048, name: 'Search' },
      { value: 735, name: 'Direct' }
    ]
  }]
}
```

---

## 🎯 Quick Reference: Make Charts Pop

| Feature | Code Snippet | Effect |
|---------|--------------|--------|
| **Gradient** | `color: { type: 'linear', colorStops: [...] }` | Modern, depth |
| **Shadow** | `shadowBlur: 10, shadowColor: '...'` | Lift, 3D effect |
| **Smooth lines** | `smooth: true` | Elegant curves |
| **Rounded bars** | `borderRadius: [5, 5, 0, 0]` | Friendly, modern |
| **Larger symbols** | `symbolSize: 10` | More visible |
| **Theme** | `theme="dark"` | Instant professional look |
| **Grid spacing** | `grid: { left: '3%', ... }` | More breathing room |
| **Emphasis** | `emphasis: { focus: 'series' }` | Better interactivity |

---

## 🔗 Essential Resources

- **Theme Builder:** https://echarts.apache.org/en/theme-builder.html
- **Official Examples:** https://echarts.apache.org/examples/en/index.html
- **Handbook:** https://echarts.apache.org/handbook/en/get-started/
- **Option Docs:** https://echarts.apache.org/en/option.html
- **echarts-for-react:** https://github.com/hustcc/echarts-for-react

---

## The Golden Rule

**Start with a theme (dark/macarons), add gradients, use useMemo, tree-shake your imports.**

That gets you 80% of the way to beautiful, performant charts!

